        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:05 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Anthony Yang",
      "case_id": "2010-09-846",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166fc160959c4234b6b89213466acb954eaf20821ad210f71c1120ec1edc5c70",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166fc160959c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court in Keene held that section 1500 of Title 28 deprives the Court Of Federal Claims has jurisdiction when the plaintiff has a pending suit in another court based on substantially the same operative facts and left open the question whether some overlap in the relief requested is also necessary to trigger that bar."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-846",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166fc160959c4234b6b89213466acb954eaf20821ad210f71c1120ec1edc5c70",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166fc160959c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But you recognize that sequential suits could be brought. So that if the case in the district court went to final judgment, then it would be okay to go to the Court Of Federal Claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Anthony Yang",
      "case_id": "2010-09-846",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166fc160959c4234b6b89213466acb954eaf20821ad210f71c1120ec1edc5c70",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166fc160959c-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. YANG: Well, it wasn't the same pot of money. The Abandoned and -- Abandoned Property Collection Act -- we will call it APCA -- provided for a special statutory trust remedy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-846",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166fc160959c4234b6b89213466acb954eaf20821ad210f71c1120ec1edc5c70",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166fc160959c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Your basic point is this: You're just saying it's too bad, go to Congress. But you don't deny the basic point, which is that an Indian tribe may think the Bureau of Indian Affairs has really mismanaged everything and what they would like is some money, and also they want an injunction so they won't do it again."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-846",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166fc160959c4234b6b89213466acb954eaf20821ad210f71c1120ec1edc5c70",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166fc160959c-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF DANIELLE SPINELLI ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
